OdooTec Development Licence

ODTL-1, version 1.4

Prepared by: OdooTec Strategy and Transformation Division
Date: 27 September 2026


1. Owner

This software, including its source code, design, data model, screens,
workflows, documentation and every modified version of it (together, "the
Module"), is the property of ODOO TEC, a limited liability company registered
in the Arab Republic of Egypt under commercial register number 125545 at the
Cairo Investment Commercial Registry Office, with its head office at Apartment
8, Building 42, Afifi Towers, Metwally El Shaarawy Street, Nasr City, Cairo
("the Owner").

In this licence, "OdooTec" means the Owner and every company the Owner owns
that supplies the Module, including Financial Center for Communication and
Information Technology, commercial register number 4030216518, Kingdom of
Saudi Arabia.

All rights not expressly granted in this licence are reserved to the Owner.


2. Scope

This licence applies to every module that OdooTec develops and supplies.

It does not apply to third-party modules, meaning modules that belong to others
and are supplied under their owners' licences. Those licences govern them.

The only modules developed by OdooTec that this licence does not apply to are
modules named individually, by module name, in a signed agreement or a signed
addendum between OdooTec and the client as owned by the client. Any module not
named in that way is covered by this licence, whatever any other document says
about the delivered work.


3. Who receives rights

Only a party holding a signed agreement with OdooTec under which the Module was
supplied ("the Client") receives rights under this licence. Anyone else holding
a copy of the Module has no right to use, run, copy, access, store or keep it,
and must delete it.


4. The Client's right of use

Once the fees due for the Module are paid, the Client may install, run and use
the Module on its own systems, for its own internal business purposes, without
time limit. This right is non-exclusive and cannot be transferred. It ends only if the Client fails to
pay fees due for the Module or breaches clause 6 or clause 7, and OdooTec gives
the Client written notice of that failure or breach.


5. People working for the Client

The Client must protect the Module as this licence requires. The Client may
allow its employees, and service providers working for it (including another
implementation partner, auditors and hosting providers), to access the Module
only to install, host, back up, maintain, support, audit or modify it for the
Client's own use.

Before giving any of them access, the Client must have each of them sign a
written undertaking addressed to OdooTec, in which they commit to OdooTec
directly to respect the Owner's ownership and copyright, the confidentiality in
clause 7 and the restrictions in clause 6. The Client must keep these
undertakings and give OdooTec a copy on request.

The Client remains responsible to OdooTec for any breach by any of them. No one
may gain any benefit from the Module other than the Client's own use of it
under this licence.


6. What is prohibited

No one, including the Client and anyone given access under clause 5, may,
without OdooTec's prior written permission:

(a) copy the Module, except the copies strictly needed for the uses that
    clauses 4 and 5 allow, which must stay under the Client's control;

(b) sell, resell, rent, lend, distribute, publish or sublicense the Module, or
    make it available to anyone not allowed by clause 5;

(c) use the Module to provide a service to anyone other than the Client;

(d) reverse engineer, decompile, analyse or study the Module to extract its
    design, logic, structure, workflows or data model, for any purpose other
    than the Client's own use;

(e) create, or help anyone create, any software that copies, reproduces,
    imitates or is substantially similar to the Module or any part of it,
    including its features, workflows, screens or data model, using the Module
    or any knowledge obtained from access to it;

(f) use the Module, any part of it, or anything derived from it, with any
    artificial intelligence or machine learning system, including to train,
    fine-tune, evaluate or prompt such a system, to generate code,
    documentation or designs, or as part of any dataset;

(g) remove or change any ownership, copyright or licence notice in the Module.


7. Confidentiality

The source code, design and documentation of the Module are OdooTec's
confidential information and trade secrets. The Client and anyone given access
under clause 5 must keep them confidential, use them only as this licence
allows, and protect them at least as carefully as they protect their own
confidential information.


8. Modification

The Client may modify the Module for its own use under clauses 4 and 5. A
modification does not give anyone ownership of the Module, and a modified
Module remains subject to this licence in full.


9. After an agreement ends

Clauses 1, 3, 5, 6, 7, 9 and 13 continue to apply after any agreement between
OdooTec and the Client ends, and after the right of use ends. If the right of
use ends under clause 4, the Client must stop using the Module and delete every
copy of it.


10. Third-party components

Some modules include or depend on software belonging to others, supplied under
its own licence. Those licences apply to those parts, and where they conflict
with this licence, they prevail for those parts only.


11. No warranty

The Module is supplied as it is. Warranties and support are only what the
signed agreement provides, and this licence implies nothing more.


12. The signed agreement

Fees, warranties and support are governed by the signed agreement. No agreement
removes a module from this licence except in the way clause 2 describes.


13. Governing law and disputes

Where the Client is established in the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia, this licence is
governed by the laws of the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia, and the courts of the
Kingdom of Saudi Arabia have jurisdiction over any dispute about it.

Where the Client is established in any other country, this licence is governed
by the laws of the Arab Republic of Egypt, and the courts of the Arab Republic
of Egypt have jurisdiction over any dispute about it.

Where the signed agreement between OdooTec and the Client provides for
arbitration, disputes between OdooTec and the Client about this licence are
resolved by that arbitration. Either of them may still ask the competent court
for urgent measures to protect confidentiality or intellectual property.


14. Version

This is ODTL-1, version 1.4. OdooTec may publish later versions. A module
carries the version named in its own files.